translated_text:
Article 7

1. The form of Women's Protection services as referred to in Article 6 letter a includes:a. legal aid;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. complaint, consultation and counseling services;

e. social reintegration services; and
f. pre-marital guidance services.
2. Pre-marital guidance services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, shall be implemented by every Woman who will enter into marriage.
3. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be conducted to provide understanding and knowledge regarding family resilience, health, psychology, religion, social and culture.
4. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's empowerment and Child Protection.
5. In implementing guidance as referred to in paragraph (4) the Regional Apparatus may involve: a. related agencies;
b. religious leaders; andc. traditional leaders.
6. Further provisions regarding the procedures for Women's Protection services shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

