translated_text:
Article 14

1. Prevention of violations of Children's rights shall be implemented by the Regional Government and the Community.
2. Prevention of violations of Children's rights implemented by the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph I]) shall be implemented by:a. establishing a work network;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Prevention based on partnership patterns with the Community, private sector, non-governmental organizations; andc. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to Child Protection.
3. Prevention of violations of Children's rights implemented by the Community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by: a. increasing Children's productivity;

b. developing Children's self-potential;
c. preventing pregnancy at a young age;
d. reducing maternal and infant mortality rates; ande. preventing the occurrence of domestic Violence.
4. Establishment of a work network as referred to in paragraph (2) letter a, includes the Regional Government's work partners in implementing Prevention of rights violations in the form of family partners.
5. Further provisions regarding Prevention of violations of Children's rights as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated in Regent Regulation.
