translated_text:
CHAPTER IV

COORDINATION AND COOPERATION

Article 16

1. Implementation of coordination and cooperation on Women's and Children's Protection aims to:a. improve efforts to fulfill the rights of Women and Children;

b. improve synergistic and harmonious working relationships; and
c. obtain data and information in the implementation of Women's and Children's Protection.

2. In order to achieve the objectives as referred to in paragraph (1) the Regional Government shall cooperate with:a. other Regional Governments;

b. related agencies;
c. non-governmental institutions;

d. universities; and
e. non-governmental organizations.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. socialization or legal counseling lectures;
c. rehabilitation of victims of Violence; andd. repatriation and social reintegration.

text:
Pasal 17

1. Pemerintah Daerah bertanggung jawab dalam perlindungan hak  Perempuan dan Anak.
2. Tanggung jawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi: - 11 -a. pendidikan;
b. kesehatan;
c. politik;
d. hukum;
e. ekonomi;
f. budaya; dang. sosial.
3. Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah terhadap perlindungan hak  Perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan:  a. penyusunan kebijakan Daerah yang responsif gender;
b. pelembagaan pengarusutamaan gender di lingkungan Pemerintah  Daerah;
c. pemberdayaan Perempuan di bidang politik, hukum, ekonomi,  budaya dan sosial pada organisasi kemasyarakatan tingkat  kabupaten;
d. penguatan dan pengembangan lembaga penyedia layanan  pemberdayaan Perempuan tingkat kabupaten;
e. melaksanakan upaya Pencegahan terjadinya Kekerasan pada  Perempuan.
4. Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah terhadap perlindungan hak  Anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan:a. perumusan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan pembangunan  Daerah yang berwawasan hak Anak yang dituangkan dalam  dokumen perencanaan pembangunan Daerah;
b. perumusan norma, standar prosedur dan kriteria penilaian  pemenuhan dan perlindungan hak Anak yang mengacu pada  norma, standar, prosedur dan kriteria yang ditetapkan  pemerintah;
c. penyelenggaraan kabupaten layak anak dilaksanakan sesua1  ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;
d. fasilitasi terselenggaranya forum Anak Daerah;
e. peningkatan peran serta Masyarakat dalam penyelenggaraan dan  perlindungan hak Anak;
f. monitoring dan evaluasi terhadap pelaksanaan program  pemenuhan dan Perlindungan Anak;
g. pembinaan lembaga Perlindungan Anak;
h. memberikan perlindungan khusus bagi Anak; dani. melaksanakan upaya Pencegahan terjadinya Kekerasan pada  Anak.

translated_text:
Article 17

1. The Regional Government is responsible for the protection of the rights of Women and Children.
2. Responsibility as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: - 11 -a. education;
b. health;
c. politics;
d. law;
e. economy;
f. culture; andg. social.
3. The Regional Government's responsibility for the protection of Women's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted by:  a. formulation of gender-responsive Regional policies;
b. institutionalization of gender mainstreaming within the Regional Government;
c. empowerment of Women in the political, legal, economic, cultural and social fields in community organizations at the regency level;
d. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Women's empowerment at the regency level;
e. implementing Prevention efforts against Violence against Women.
4. The Regional Government's responsibility for the protection of Children's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted by:a. formulation of policies, programs, and Regional development activities with a child rights perspective that are set forth in Regional development planning documents;
b. formulation of norms, standard procedures and assessment criteria for the fulfillment and protection of Children's rights that refer to norms, standards, procedures and criteria established by the government;
c. implementation of child-friendly regency shall be carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
d. facilitation of the implementation of Regional Children's forum;
e. increasing Community participation in the implementation and protection of Children's rights;
f. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of Children's fulfillment and Protection programs;
g. guidance of Child Protection institutions;
h. providing special protection for Children; andi. implementing Prevention efforts against Violence against Children.

