Article 21

1. The technical service institution as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (2) letter a shall be implemented by P2TP2A and FPK2PA.
2. In organizing the Protection of Women and Children, the Regional Government shall establish a regional technical implementing unit for Protection of Women and Children.
3. The establishment of the regional technical implementing unit as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation after obtaining written approval from the Governor.
4. In the case of implementing technical services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish a task force.
(5) The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) may also carry out institutional strengthening through cooperation and coordination with: a. CFC task force;
b. CRA task force;
c. K/DRA task force;
d. schools and/or educational institutions;
e. Children's forum;
f. children's center;
g. community organizations;
h. Women's organizations; and i. other institutions concerned with the fulfillment of rights and Protection of Children.
6. The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) constitutes a coordinative institution at the district and sub-district level that coordinates policies, programs and activities to realize sub-districts, child-friendly villages/wards.
7. Further provisions regarding technical services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

